# The repository is LF-only: .editorconfig declares `end_of_line = lf` and the Prettier
# config declares `endOfLine: 'lf'`. Without this file neither of those declarations reaches
# git, so Git for Windows applies its system-wide `core.autocrlf=true` and checks every file
# out with CRLF -- at which point `prettier --check` fails on the whole tree and the
# `pnpm check` gate is unreproducible for anyone on Windows. This makes git honour what the
# repository already says about itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
